<title>CHINA: Shanghai Jintai 96 loses 6.86 mln yuan.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Jintai 96 loses 6.86 mln yuan.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of yuan unless stated, against 1995 figures)</p>
<p> Turnover	     162.767</p>
<p> Net profit	    (6.863)</p>
<p> Net asset per share     1.97   yuan</p>
<p> Earnings per share     (0.037) yuan</p>
<p>Company name: Shanghai Jintai Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The company did not give comparative figures. It was listed on the Shanghai stock exchange in July 1995, and last year only posted results for the second half of the year.</p>
<p>Note: the results were published in a company statement on Tuesday. The numbers are based on domestic accounting standards. Figures based on international accounting standards were not available.</p>
<p>The company's board of directors proposed no cash dividend or bonus issue, pending approval of a shareholders' meeting.</p>
</text>
